{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1794858276048080857,"compiled_state":{"alias":"leafy-gorillian-gnat","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"ad44437d2748b7673181804cc001c92ec53496c6794c98ae34b3972b9573d797","event_uuid":"9d91f75b-79a7-4ad8-b315-4e01b5c16d58","position":{"commit_sha":"a2024631b777fe5d8cdd4b9e5393582d00cd5ec4","position":"1794857684450297674-9d91f75b-79a7-4ad8-b315-4e01b5c16d58"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"30a7bb3573e67a76823f96dbe496dfbc5d4b9739f51d6f2ac16bdca642b23a9d","event_uuid":"1b8c6498-b539-44b3-9034-51c5c3fd6663","position":{"commit_sha":"550dd17c044241a61ca0c70c121d624bbfd7c46a","position":"1794857767482011006-1b8c6498-b539-44b3-9034-51c5c3fd6663"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"359471edc14cd56d67c50b0e34821b28481b48667e5cb786faa6f3413ddfeae5","event_uuid":"10aaef00-7b6f-413d-9d8e-9cfc322e5505","position":{"commit_sha":"b7aa728bc2d2b1e2b0abd723014a0eeb4ca528c3","position":"1794858276048080856-10aaef00-7b6f-413d-9d8e-9cfc322e5505"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Starting evidence (read from source at b4e0d01b649, not yet tested on Windows): the product-side literal is the read-freshness throttle marker in `src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py` `_sync_marker_age` (`f\"/tmp/.ticket-sync-{md5[:12]}\"`), opened for read there and for write later in `ensure_fresh`. On Windows `/tmp` is drive-relative and usually absent, so the read returns age 9999 and the write fails inside the best-effort `except`, which would mean the 60-second fetch throttle never engages and every read fetches. Test-side copies of the literal: `tests/unit/test_read_freshness_git_spawns.py:99`, `tests/unit/test_read_freshness_parity.py:139`, `tests/unit/test_compact_fold_prelock.py:152`, `tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py:91`, `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_fresh_ac_material.py:47`, `tests/interfaces/store/sync_contention_harness.py:46`. Design point for the fix: `tempfile.gettempdir()` honours `TMPDIR`, so two processes with different `TMPDIR` would stop sharing one throttle on POSIX; a marker under the tracker's git dir avoids that. Expose the path through one helper the tests import instead of re-deriving it.","timestamp":1794858276048080856}],"created_at":1794857684450297674,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"1b8c6498-b539-44b3-9034-51c5c3fd6663","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6798-606d-37dc-46e7"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job runs a maintained subset held green: tests known to fail on Windows are deselected through `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/hardcoded-tmp.args`. This bug owns that file: 21 tests in 5 modules, from the 5 scheduled runs at `b4e0d01b649` (2026-11-15/16).\n\nCode or tests build `/tmp/.ticket-sync-<hash>` and similar literal paths. On Windows `/tmp` is drive-relative and absent, so they fail with `FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '\\\\tmp\\\\.ticket-sync-<hash>'` (18) or compare `'\\\\tmp\\\\foo'` with `'/tmp/foo'`.\n\nModules: `tests/unit/test_read_freshness_git_spawns.py` (8), `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_fresh_ac_material.py` (6), `tests/unit/test_read_freshness_parity.py` (5), `tests/unit/reconciler/state/test_sync_logger.py` (1), `tests/unit/test_child_hooks.py` (1).\n\n## Approach\n\nFind where `.ticket-sync-<hash>` is built (product or fixture). Use `tempfile.gettempdir()` in product code or `tmp_path` in tests instead of a literal `/tmp`, and compare paths as `Path` objects.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe failing product or test code for this class, plus `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/hardcoded-tmp.args` (remove each fixed line; delete the file and its `@` reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml` once empty).\n\n## Testing\n\nPOSIX: the touched tests still pass under `make verify`. Windows: a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the change passes with the removed lines no longer deselected.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The class's root cause is recorded on this ticket with the evidence that confirmed it.\n- [ ] Every line removed from `hardcoded-tmp.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on that run.\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["windows","portability"],"ticket_id":"c1cf-bf46-01a9-4b17","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Windows sweep: literal /tmp paths (21 tests)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9d91f75b-79a7-4ad8-b315-4e01b5c16d58","1b8c6498-b539-44b3-9034-51c5c3fd6663","10aaef00-7b6f-413d-9d8e-9cfc322e5505"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794858276048080857,"uuid":"e37693c1-abbb-4aaf-b419-1b7bd7df62f3"}
